'''Castello''', officially '''Castello del Mare''' ([[Italian language|Italian]] for "Castle of the Sea") is a [[w:Smart city|smart city]] or "ubiquitous city" built from scratch on {{convert|3200|acre}} of [[w:Land reclamation|reclaimed land]] in the narrow Augustian Sea, {{convert|30|km}} northwest of [[Alessandria]], [[Cordova]] and connected to the Baliscan and Siculian mainlands by the {{convert|55|km}}  [[Baliscan-Siculian Friendship Bridge]]. Along with the newly reclaimed [[Capua]] and [[Nola]], it is part of the [[Augusta Free Economic Zone]]. It is a [[w:Condominium (international law)|condominium]], and is governed jointly by the Baliscan Confederation and the Federal Republic of Siculia, with additional provisions to residents including total ownership over property and independent utility management, which reduces tax overhead. It is a major [[Atlántida|Atlántido]] port and is considered an {{W|satellite city|accessory city}} to the larger [[Augusta Corridor]]. It is the the # largest city overall in [[Cordova]] and the [[List of largest Baliscan cities by population|# most populated]] city in Balisca, with a population of 521,908 as of 2022.

